  "author_known_issues": [
    {
      "heading": "Warnings, Precautions, and Limitations",
      "line": 813,
      "text": "## Warnings and precautions - Use the loci file version that matches the reference genome passed to --ref. - Haplotagged input is recommended. If --bypass-haplotag-check is used, close-in-length alleles may be merged and accuracy may be reduced. - If using non-standard --loci, check the BED file carefully before use. - If a TR region contains sequence that is not actually repetitive, motif decomposition of this unexpected sequence may be effectively nonsensical. The reported length in bases is still meaningful. - Previous versions of mahi-mahi have used different parameters, configurations, an",
      "truncated": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/nanoporetech/mahi-mahi/blob/861ea09ab44e88424c45b04d8018f3948a8fefbb/README.md#L813"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Warnings and precautions",
      "line": 815,
      "text": "- Use the loci file version that matches the reference genome passed to --ref. - Haplotagged input is recommended. If --bypass-haplotag-check is used, close-in-length alleles may be merged and accuracy may be reduced. - If using non-standard --loci, check the BED file carefully before use. - If a TR region contains sequence that is not actually repetitive, motif decomposition of this unexpected sequence may be effectively nonsensical. The reported length in bases is still meaningful. - Previous versions of mahi-mahi have used different parameters, configurations, and filenames. Please refer to",
      "truncated": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/nanoporetech/mahi-mahi/blob/861ea09ab44e88424c45b04d8018f3948a8fefbb/README.md#L815"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Known limitations",
      "line": 827,
      "text": "- When the original BAM contains many non-spanning reads, `DP` can be lower than an allele's `AD` or the sum of `AD`. `DP` measures mean alignment depth over the reference repeat interval, whereas `AD` counts reads selected for allele-length estimation, including selected non-spanning reads. This difference does not by itself indicate an invalid call. - Expansions supported mainly by non-spanning reads may be underestimated and sized less precisely than fully spanned alleles. - Apparent interruptions may be sequencing errors. Visual verification using the read visualisation is recommended. - I",
      "truncated": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/nanoporetech/mahi-mahi/blob/861ea09ab44e88424c45b04d8018f3948a8fefbb/README.md#L827"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Troubleshooting and Support",
      "line": 891,
      "text": "For help, contact Oxford Nanopore Technologies through your usual support channel: [Oxford Nanopore customer support](https://nanoporetech.com/support/customer-support). ## Common checks - Confirm that the reference genome matches the loci file. - Confirm that the BAM or CRAM file is readable and indexed. - Confirm that the sample sex argument is correct. - Confirm that the input BAM is haplotagged unless --bypass-haplotag-check is intentionally being used. ## Common problems and messages | Message or issue | Likely cause | Suggested action | |------------------------|------------------------|",
      "truncated": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/nanoporetech/mahi-mahi/blob/861ea09ab44e88424c45b04d8018f3948a8fefbb/README.md#L891"
    }
  ],
